This looks like a CBP ruling on a decorative pillow shaped like a dog or cat. The question is whether it is a cushion (9404.90) or a festive article (9505.90). It is a Day of the Dead decorative pillow, so festive articles under 9505 are plausible. Cushions are classified in 9404.90, but CBP has treated pillows with a holiday theme as festive articles in some rulings (for example, Halloween pillows in 9505.90.6000). A Day of the Dead pillow sold around the holiday is likely treated the same way.

The alternative is a stuffed toy under 9503.00.0090, but these are decorative pillows rather than toys. Day of the Dead is a recognized holiday, and the "festive, carnival or other entertainment articles" heading covers articles associated with it. The 9505.90.6000 subheading is "Other: Other" for festive articles, so I'll use that.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "The decorative pillows are printed with a Day of the Dead motif and sold around that holiday, so they are festive articles of heading 9505 rather than ordinary cushions of heading 9404."}
